    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea2d7ab0_124c5fc9",
        "filename": "Tethering/src/android/net/ip/IpServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 1436,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-01T07:21:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion: this is now necessary because cleanupUpstream no longer clears downstream rules. But if so, I think this cleanup code needs to be in TetheredState#exit, not here. I don\u0027t think we should keep any rules while we are not in TetheredState.\n\nOne example of how this might be incorrect is that if the IpServer goes into InitialState but we do not delete the rules, then we never process CMD_IPV6_TETHER_UPDATE and we never change the upstream interface index in the downstream rules. This is probably not too bad, but it\u0027s just an example.\n\n\nI think you mentioned a concern that if we stop tethering and then restart it, then the neighbour entries will still be in the kernel\u0027s ND cache, and therefore when tethering is restarted, downstream offload won\u0027t work? But if so, I think:\n1. We already have this problem today because whenever cleanupUpstream runs, all rules are deleted, but no ND cache entries are deleted.\n2. The problem likely fixes itself after a while: when the software path forwards to the neighbour, the ND cache entry will eventually get into STALE then DELAY then REACHABLE, and one of those events will send a NeighborEvent and recreate the rule.\n3. If we want to fix this we should probably make the NeighbourMonitor send a netlink dump for neighbours (e.g., in startIpv6()).\n\nI think similar comments apply to the call to mIpNeighborMonitor.stop().\n\nFor now I think it would be good to move this to TetheredState#exit, so that when tethering stops, all upstream and downstream rules are deleted. After that CL is merged we can do #3 above in a follow-up.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1436,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 1436,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0a973f7b39e75cf0a953a22c83794d7181316359",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
